00:35:07.350 --> 00:35:08.994
Makes you feel a little better about it.

00:35:08.994 --> 00:35:11.100
Well you could find a way
to catch 'em and eat 'em.

00:35:11.100 --> 00:35:12.603
I'm not that hungry.

00:35:14.280 --> 00:35:16.140
You could probably find
some recipes on TikTok

00:35:16.140 --> 00:35:18.090
for mole stew or something.

00:35:18.090 --> 00:35:20.883
Put 'em in that nicely oiled skillet.

00:35:24.270 --> 00:35:26.010
This purchase comes with a story.

00:35:26.010 --> 00:35:30.750
I bought four items, two
Carolina Panthers hats

00:35:30.750 --> 00:35:32.523
and two Carolina Panthers shirts.

00:35:33.480 --> 00:35:36.630
I remember seeing you wearing this once

00:35:36.630 --> 00:35:38.460
and it was just one of those
things where it's like-

00:35:38.460 --> 00:35:39.780
You didn't ask any questions.

00:35:39.780 --> 00:35:41.080
I thought I told you this.

00:35:42.090 --> 00:35:43.478
So-

00:35:43.478 --> 00:35:45.317
Is this a James And The Shame?

00:35:45.317 --> 00:35:46.200
Yes.

00:35:46.200 --> 00:35:49.800
So I had a PR person working on

00:35:49.800 --> 00:35:52.530
right around the launch
of the album with me

00:35:52.530 --> 00:35:55.080
on some press opportunities.

00:35:55.080 --> 00:35:59.490
And one of them was, I
guess it was Spin Magazine.

00:35:59.490 --> 00:36:04.320
It has this thing where they
do musicians give predictions

00:36:04.320 --> 00:36:06.690
for their favorite team's NFL season.

00:36:06.690 --> 00:36:07.800
And she was like, would you be interested?

00:36:07.800 --> 00:36:09.480
Do you watch NFL?

00:36:09.480 --> 00:36:10.920
Do you have a favorite team

00:36:10.920 --> 00:36:11.753
and would you be willing to do this?

00:36:11.753 --> 00:36:14.910
And I was like, yes.

00:36:14.910 --> 00:36:16.170
A little bit.

00:36:16.170 --> 00:36:18.300
And then to the second question,

00:36:18.300 --> 00:36:21.390
I mean I'm an NC State football fan,

00:36:21.390 --> 00:36:23.400
I like college football
and that's what I watch.

00:36:23.400 --> 00:36:27.900
But I consider myself a Rams
fan being in Los Angeles.

00:36:27.900 --> 00:36:29.220
But I have a, you know,

00:36:29.220 --> 00:36:31.590
an affinity for the Carolina Panthers

00:36:31.590 --> 00:36:33.360
only because they're in North Carolina.

00:36:33.360 --> 00:36:35.880
But I don't really keep up with it

00:36:35.880 --> 00:36:38.010
and I don't own any fan gear.

00:36:38.010 --> 00:36:40.494
So what I said is, yes, I'm willing to do-

00:36:40.494 --> 00:36:41.327
You can't say that.

00:36:41.327 --> 00:36:42.930
Yes, I'm willing to do this

00:36:42.930 --> 00:36:45.930
and I can do either the
Rams or the Panthers.

00:36:45.930 --> 00:36:47.730
I feel like there's probably somebody else

00:36:47.730 --> 00:36:50.370
already representing the Rams, so yes.

00:36:50.370 --> 00:36:51.540
And I'm like, the reason I'm doing this

00:36:51.540 --> 00:36:53.853
is because of the press opportunity.

00:36:54.810 --> 00:36:55.643
So I did it.

00:36:55.643 --> 00:36:56.476
It's all an illusion.

00:36:56.476 --> 00:36:58.350
So the first thing I needed to do was

00:36:59.940 --> 00:37:01.233
you know, get clothes.

00:37:02.881 --> 00:37:04.650
I don't, I mean I don't
even wear NC States-

00:37:04.650 --> 00:37:06.120
Cause they were putting a picture of you?

00:37:06.120 --> 00:37:09.780
Yeah, they wanted a picture
of me in Ram's gear.

00:37:09.780 --> 00:37:11.910
I mean in Carolina Panther's gear.

00:37:11.910 --> 00:37:13.083
So I had to find some.

00:37:14.236 --> 00:37:18.720
Well based on what I saw
of you wearing that stuff,

00:37:18.720 --> 00:37:21.240
I don't know if it's a
great PR opportunity.

00:37:21.240 --> 00:37:24.240
I'm just telling you, I mean,
you looked like a dork dude.

00:37:24.240 --> 00:37:27.720
Well, can I just say,
and I hate to say this,

00:37:27.720 --> 00:37:32.720
but it's very difficult to
dress up in support of your team

00:37:33.240 --> 00:37:34.380
and not look like a dork.

00:37:34.380 --> 00:37:35.250
I know.

00:37:35.250 --> 00:37:36.083
And I gotta-

00:37:36.083 --> 00:37:37.211
It's like you're cosplaying

00:37:37.211 --> 00:37:40.497
as what everyone thinks a fan is.

00:37:40.497 --> 00:37:42.990
Aren't there people who are fans of sports

00:37:42.990 --> 00:37:45.150
that also like to look cool?

00:37:45.150 --> 00:37:47.670
You can, for some reason-

00:37:47.670 --> 00:37:49.773
I have a theory. This is it.

00:37:51.240 --> 00:37:54.750
They make the stuff out
of the same material

00:37:54.750 --> 00:37:57.840
that they make athletic
clothing out of a lot of times.

00:37:57.840 --> 00:38:02.460
So these t-shirts had this
moisture wicking dry fit.

00:38:02.460 --> 00:38:05.289
So much of this stuff has this-

00:38:05.289 --> 00:38:07.110
In case you need to go out there.

00:38:07.110 --> 00:38:09.266
Well these people are
just watching sports guys.

00:38:09.266 --> 00:38:10.099
On the field.

00:38:10.099 --> 00:38:12.510
Like when you go watch a concert,

00:38:12.510 --> 00:38:16.290
you can get a cool t-shirt
that is like a cotton t-shirt

00:38:16.290 --> 00:38:18.480
or like a 50 50 t-shirt.

00:38:18.480 --> 00:38:20.100
You can get a cool hat

00:38:20.100 --> 00:38:23.673
that looks like someone who
is ready to watch something.

00:38:24.720 --> 00:38:27.390
Fans of athletic performances

00:38:27.390 --> 00:38:29.040
should be able to wear the same things

00:38:29.040 --> 00:38:31.080
that fans of musical performances wear.

00:38:31.080 --> 00:38:32.507
You're not playing.

00:38:32.507 --> 00:38:33.810
Hey, hey, you need to shut up.

00:38:33.810 --> 00:38:35.493
This is a business opportunity.

00:38:36.450 --> 00:38:38.580
We need to keep this to ourself
till we're ready to launch.

00:38:38.580 --> 00:38:39.840
They just don't make any cool,

00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:41.550
they don't make enough cool stuff.

00:38:41.550 --> 00:38:44.883
Even I would wear more
NC State stuff. I would.

00:38:46.110 --> 00:38:47.662
It is just like a needle in a haystack

00:38:47.662 --> 00:38:50.070
to find a shirt that's cool.

00:38:51.060 --> 00:38:56.060
The retro logoing is one
particular avenue to coolness.

00:38:57.660 --> 00:38:59.070
Even when they brought back.
Well NC State hasn't-

00:38:59.070 --> 00:39:00.750
They brought that back.

00:39:00.750 --> 00:39:02.250
Yeah, they brought back the wolf,

00:39:02.250 --> 00:39:04.710
but then the stuff that they put it on,

00:39:04.710 --> 00:39:07.233
it's like they're still
in this athletic mode.

00:39:08.190 --> 00:39:09.960
What do you guys think I'm doing?

00:39:09.960 --> 00:39:13.050
I'm sitting on a couch and
then standing up at moments

00:39:13.050 --> 00:39:15.258
and then sitting back down on the couch.

00:39:15.258 --> 00:39:16.380
I don't need

00:39:16.380 --> 00:39:17.997
moisture wicking material here
And now posing for a photo

00:39:17.997 --> 00:39:19.410
for Spin Magazine.

00:39:19.410 --> 00:39:21.600
So what did you look,
I never saw this photo.

00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:22.590
Did it happen?

00:39:22.590 --> 00:39:26.130
Oh yeah, it was just a
selfie. I took it in there.

00:39:26.130 --> 00:39:28.290
You were wearing what? A jersey?

00:39:28.290 --> 00:39:30.930
No, I wore a T-shirt and a hat.

00:39:30.930 --> 00:39:34.680
But even that still felt like,
this doesn't feel like me.

00:39:34.680 --> 00:39:37.080
But I mean that's what they wanted.

00:39:37.080 --> 00:39:38.490
The other piece of this puzzle is

00:39:38.490 --> 00:39:41.190
I had to come up with my prediction

00:39:41.190 --> 00:39:43.503
for the Carolina Panther season.

00:39:44.430 --> 00:39:48.750
So at that point I just texted my dad

00:39:48.750 --> 00:39:52.260
and said, "Dad, a
research project for you,

00:39:52.260 --> 00:39:54.000
newly retired man."

00:39:54.000 --> 00:39:56.280
Who also doesn't care that
much about NFL football,

00:39:56.280 --> 00:39:59.580
but likes college football in Georgia.

00:39:59.580 --> 00:40:01.830
He quickly like just came back with-

00:40:01.830 --> 00:40:04.170
He's your ghost writer.
Here's what I think.

00:40:04.170 --> 00:40:06.540
And now I will say that
if you read the article,

00:40:06.540 --> 00:40:08.760
any funny parts of it-

00:40:08.760 --> 00:40:09.593
Your dad wrote.

00:40:09.593 --> 00:40:11.190
I wrote, because my dad
didn't make it funny.

00:40:11.190 --> 00:40:13.800
It was very much just,
here's bullet points,

00:40:13.800 --> 00:40:16.831
including my obsession
with the long snapper.

00:40:16.831 --> 00:40:18.800
I added that.
Okay.

00:40:18.800 --> 00:40:20.270
So the long snapper stuff

00:40:20.270 --> 00:40:22.920
because I am genuinely
interested in long snappers

00:40:22.920 --> 00:40:25.385
and the Johansen, I think his name is,

00:40:25.385 --> 00:40:28.710
played 16 seasons without
missing a game or something.

00:40:28.710 --> 00:40:30.123
Anyway, so yeah,

00:40:30.995 --> 00:40:33.240
if you ever need any
Carolina Panthers stuff,

00:40:33.240 --> 00:40:34.470
I got two hats and two shirts.

00:40:34.470 --> 00:40:35.303
We could go out together.

00:40:35.303 --> 00:40:37.650
That you will never wear again.

00:40:37.650 --> 00:40:39.409
Yeah, also, I'm kind of-

00:40:39.409 --> 00:40:40.770
Did anything come from it?

00:40:40.770 --> 00:40:43.980
Did you get any listens
from Caroline Panthers fans

00:40:43.980 --> 00:40:46.830
that you're now completely
undermining with this story?

00:40:46.830 --> 00:40:48.090
Well, I think the name of the article was

00:40:48.090 --> 00:40:53.090
56 Musicians Predict Their
Take on their NFL season.

00:40:55.980 --> 00:40:56.823
Who else?

00:40:57.810 --> 00:40:58.950
Some people that you would recognize

00:40:58.950 --> 00:41:01.170
and a lot of people that you wouldn't.

00:41:01.170 --> 00:41:03.930
So maybe I got one listen from that.

00:41:03.930 --> 00:41:04.763
It was worth it.

00:41:06.000 --> 00:41:07.740
That's the world of PR man.

00:41:07.740 --> 00:41:08.573
Oh yeah.

00:41:08.573 --> 00:41:09.406
Oh my gosh.

00:41:11.778 --> 00:41:14.343
Here's a good one, sweet one.

00:41:16.230 --> 00:41:20.043
Where the Sidewalk Ends, the book.

00:41:20.910 --> 00:41:21.743
I'm familiar with it.

00:41:21.743 --> 00:41:25.303
Shell Silverstein and
I didn't write it down,

00:41:27.090 --> 00:41:32.090
but also we got a bunch of
our favorite, you know, kids-

00:41:33.960 --> 00:41:35.430
Kids' books.

00:41:35.430 --> 00:41:36.690
A couple of Shell Silversteins,

00:41:36.690 --> 00:41:40.863
like the Light in the Attic,
Where the Wild Things Are.

00:41:42.300 --> 00:41:43.620
And this was-

00:41:43.620 --> 00:41:44.790
Did you get the issue of Playboy

00:41:44.790 --> 00:41:45.660
with his famous interview?

00:41:45.660 --> 00:41:46.950
Did you also get that?

00:41:46.950 --> 00:41:48.808
Uh uh, uh uh.

00:41:48.808 --> 00:41:49.641
That would've been a nice touch.

00:41:49.641 --> 00:41:51.240
Yeah Shell Silverstein.

00:41:51.240 --> 00:41:53.550
He wrote a boy named Sue for Johnny Cash.

00:41:53.550 --> 00:41:57.330
He's was in that world,
the outlaw country world.

00:41:57.330 --> 00:41:59.613
Anyway, but cool thing.

00:42:00.780 --> 00:42:02.910
This was in honor of-

00:42:02.910 --> 00:42:04.113
Maybe you've seen these,

00:42:05.790 --> 00:42:08.100
if you take a walk with
your dog in a neighborhood

00:42:08.100 --> 00:42:09.810
or if you go to certain parts of town,

00:42:09.810 --> 00:42:12.690
you can see there's
these little libraries.

00:42:12.690 --> 00:42:14.490
They look like a bird box.

00:42:14.490 --> 00:42:18.270
But it's a library where
you can exchange books.

00:42:18.270 --> 00:42:21.000
You can put a book in, take a book out.

00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:25.500
And Christie did this with,

00:42:25.500 --> 00:42:30.500
well, her sister Britney
and JB, they ordered

00:42:31.440 --> 00:42:35.070
and then her dad, Bobby, my father-in-law

00:42:35.070 --> 00:42:37.350
built one of these boxes

00:42:37.350 --> 00:42:39.497
and then they painted it custom color

00:42:39.497 --> 00:42:42.180
and they put the plaque on it

00:42:42.180 --> 00:42:45.600
and they put it up in
honor of their, you know,

00:42:45.600 --> 00:42:48.250
their first daughter passed away

00:42:49.260 --> 00:42:51.150
hours after being born.

00:42:51.150 --> 00:42:53.760
And she would've been 10 years old,

00:42:53.760 --> 00:42:56.490
Sayla would've been 10
years old this year.

00:42:56.490 --> 00:43:00.930
So every year they celebrate her life

00:43:00.930 --> 00:43:05.760
and then their other kids,

00:43:05.760 --> 00:43:07.470
they now have two more kids.

00:43:07.470 --> 00:43:09.750
I got a niece and a nephew.

00:43:09.750 --> 00:43:12.833
They, you know, they learn about Sayla

00:43:12.833 --> 00:43:16.410
and the story of, even
through all of that pain

00:43:16.410 --> 00:43:21.410
that it's become something
that's been very beautiful,

00:43:24.540 --> 00:43:26.790
you know, in honoring her memory.

00:43:26.790 --> 00:43:31.790
So for her 10th birthday, they
created one of these boxes.

00:43:33.840 --> 00:43:36.600
So we were able to buy book books for it

00:43:36.600 --> 00:43:37.433
and we were actually-

00:43:37.433 --> 00:43:38.266
Did they put it up in the neighborhood

00:43:38.266 --> 00:43:39.099
or did they put it up in
front of their house or?

00:43:39.099 --> 00:43:43.200
They put it up in
Lilington at the ballpark,

00:43:43.200 --> 00:43:46.710
you know where you and
I did the 4th of July.

00:43:46.710 --> 00:43:48.092
Where they do the fireworks every year.

00:43:48.092 --> 00:43:50.670
That's where I played
baseball hundreds of time.

00:43:50.670 --> 00:43:54.393
And where we did our 4th of
July Wax Paper Dogs concert.

00:43:55.440 --> 00:43:57.480
Yeah, they actually put it up there.

00:43:57.480 --> 00:44:02.220
And because we went back
for Lance's wedding,

00:44:02.220 --> 00:44:06.330
we were there for the ribbon cutting.

00:44:06.330 --> 00:44:08.190
So we were able to put the books in there

00:44:08.190 --> 00:44:10.680
and honor Sayla's life and memory

00:44:10.680 --> 00:44:14.910
and it was a great family
moment to be a part of that.

00:44:14.910 --> 00:44:19.910
And yeah, I wrote down the name of the...

00:44:20.392 --> 00:44:23.280
littlefreelibrary.org.

00:44:23.280 --> 00:44:24.630
Oh. So you can just make one?

00:44:24.630 --> 00:44:25.643
There's a number of places
If you register it?

00:44:25.643 --> 00:44:27.060
That will do it.

00:44:27.060 --> 00:44:29.910
But if you go to little free library.org,

00:44:29.910 --> 00:44:32.550
you can order the pieces
and they'll send it to you

00:44:32.550 --> 00:44:35.610
and you can build it
and paint it yourself.

00:44:35.610 --> 00:44:39.930
And then they'll send you
like the plaque to put on it

00:44:39.930 --> 00:44:42.940
so that in their case it can say

00:44:45.627 --> 00:44:47.700
'In honor of Sayla'.

00:44:47.700 --> 00:44:49.830
And then, you know, it
is part of the community

00:44:49.830 --> 00:44:53.460
and it looks really cool and nice

00:44:53.460 --> 00:44:55.410
and of course they got
permission from the ballpark

00:44:55.410 --> 00:44:57.030
to put it there.

00:44:57.030 --> 00:44:58.050
That's awesome.

00:44:58.050 --> 00:45:00.603
So yeah, littlefreelibrary.org,

00:45:01.530 --> 00:45:03.750
and you can do it for
whatever reason you want

00:45:03.750 --> 00:45:05.550
or just do it to contribute
to your community.

00:45:05.550 --> 00:45:09.097
But there's lots of kids
who are taking walks

00:45:09.097 --> 00:45:11.100
or like, "Hey, let's go to that library.

00:45:11.100 --> 00:45:12.390
Let's see what books are in there now.

00:45:12.390 --> 00:45:14.970
Let's put some of my
favorite books in there."

00:45:14.970 --> 00:45:16.440
You think kids are doing that?

00:45:16.440 --> 00:45:17.310
Yeah, definitely.

00:45:17.310 --> 00:45:18.840
Kids still got books?

00:45:18.840 --> 00:45:19.800
Yeah, that's the thing.

00:45:19.800 --> 00:45:21.000
It's kind of this retro thing

00:45:21.000 --> 00:45:23.670
that gives you a sense of connection

00:45:23.670 --> 00:45:26.087
and being a part of
something in real life.

00:45:26.087 --> 00:45:28.800
Unless you vandalize it.

00:45:28.800 --> 00:45:31.036
Yeah, I mean this is
in a good place where-

00:45:31.036 --> 00:45:33.090
It only takes one.

00:45:33.090 --> 00:45:34.983
Yeah. Sadly that's true.

00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:37.743
When you talk about that place,

00:45:38.640 --> 00:45:41.160
the Lilington ball fields there.

00:45:41.160 --> 00:45:42.240
Yeah.

00:45:42.240 --> 00:45:45.360
They're so nostalgic to
me because of the smell,

00:45:45.360 --> 00:45:49.530
which it was a mix of dirt, grass, popcorn

00:45:49.530 --> 00:45:53.760
and cigarette smoke that I
felt like I smelled repeatedly

00:45:53.760 --> 00:45:56.160
as a child playing outdoor sports

00:45:56.160 --> 00:45:59.430
that was so pronounced at
that particular location

00:45:59.430 --> 00:46:01.050
that I'm sure it doesn't smell as much

00:46:01.050 --> 00:46:02.160
like cigarette smoke anymore

00:46:02.160 --> 00:46:05.060
because it's just so much less
common for people to smoke.

00:46:06.521 --> 00:46:09.210
Well the other cool part
of it was that morning,

00:46:09.210 --> 00:46:10.440
our nephew Nehemiah,

00:46:10.440 --> 00:46:13.590
he had a soccer game there on the field.

00:46:13.590 --> 00:46:17.610
So we watched him play and
then we dedicated the library,

00:46:17.610 --> 00:46:20.790
took some pictures, but I was like,

00:46:20.790 --> 00:46:22.920
yeah, it's wild to come back here.

00:46:22.920 --> 00:46:26.520
I was telling, you know,
telling Lincoln Orlando,

00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:28.770
I played T-ball on these fields,

00:46:28.770 --> 00:46:32.038
but you know, because I hated T-ball.

00:46:32.038 --> 00:46:33.990
It makes you feel anxious
when you see the fields?

00:46:33.990 --> 00:46:36.963
Yeah. I was like, my butt
hole was getting real tight.

00:46:38.040 --> 00:46:43.040
So yeah, I choose to think more
about all of the fireworks.

00:46:43.110 --> 00:46:44.170
That's what I associate
with the fireworks.

00:46:44.170 --> 00:46:45.630
We do fireworks here.

00:46:45.630 --> 00:46:46.780
Fireworks every year.

00:46:48.210 --> 00:46:49.530
Okay, here's the next one from me.

00:46:49.530 --> 00:46:54.000
Five pack USB wall charger
and five pack charger cables.

00:46:54.000 --> 00:46:55.380
Oh yeah.

00:46:55.380 --> 00:46:59.910
This has to be an annual re-up.

00:46:59.910 --> 00:47:02.497
I just feel like, again, I don't want to,

00:47:02.497 --> 00:47:04.983
I'm gonna go into the dad mode.

00:47:06.390 --> 00:47:11.040
So the thing I have asked for is,

00:47:11.040 --> 00:47:14.430
so I have a charger next to my bed right?

00:47:14.430 --> 00:47:15.450
For my phone.

00:47:15.450 --> 00:47:18.030
It is a wireless charger
that I can set my phone on

00:47:18.030 --> 00:47:20.640
and I can also put my AirPods on

00:47:20.640 --> 00:47:21.890
and they can both charge.

00:47:23.430 --> 00:47:26.370
And then Jesse uses a
traditional just USB cable

00:47:26.370 --> 00:47:28.620
that plugs directly into her phone.

